f=3D"https://www.pyimagesearch.com/2017/04/03/facial-landmarks-dlib-opencv-=
python/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer noopener" aria-label=3D"detect=
 facial landmarks (opens in a new tab)">detect facial landmarks</a> using d=
lib so that we know where to place a mask on the face.</figcaption></figure=
></div>



<p>Next, we need an image of a mask (with a transparent background) such as=
